  "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $G$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $G$ where every element of $G$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only ${{10,15,35},{20},{25,30}}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- ${\u2205,{10,15,35},{20},{25,30}}$ is not a partition because the subset $\u2205$ is empty.\n\n- ${{10,15,25,35},{20,25,30}}$ is not a partition because the element $25$ appears in two subsets.\n\n- ${{10,15,20,30},{20,30},{25,35,30}}$ is not a partition because the elements $20$ and $30$ appear in multiple subsets.\n\n- ${{15,20,25,30,35}}$ is not a partition because the element $10\\in G$ does not appear in any subset.",
